{"title":"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On February 13 <i>The Oshkosh Northwester</i> listed the length of daylight as 10 hours and 24 minutes, the sunrise was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/8080002e6149ec61ef9830af5e2f136728452db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6:57\\textsc{am}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" />, and the sunset as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f551194b9b3e0d9696135e5bcdfee5c1285d09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8:15\\textsc{pm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />. The length of daylight and sunrise were correct, but the sunset was wrong. When did the sun really set?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386b03847ea3c24034939261f08bcf2e5122e38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\hspace{.05in}5:10\\textsc{pm}\\quad\\textbf{(B)}\\hspace{.05in}5:21\\textsc{pm}\\quad\\textbf{(C)}\\hspace{.05in}5:41\\textsc{pm}\\quad\\textbf{(D)}\\hspace{.05in}5:57\\textsc{pm}\\quad\\textbf{(E)}\\hspace{.05in}6:03\\textsc{pm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"559\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem wants us to find the time of sunset and gives us the length of daylight and time of sunrise. So all we have to do is add the length of daylight to the time of sunrise to obtain the answer. Convert 10 hours and 24 minutes into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d40930ee7b45d218b3c707ca0413a7b9e1cdfdd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10:24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> in order to add easier.\n</p><p>Adding, we find that the time of sunset is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/0/99008001d24c3799734028d3751556c777a0ea4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6:57\\textsc{am} + 10:24 \\implies 17:21 \\implies  \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5:21\\textsc{pm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"399\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The length of daylight is 10 hours and 24 minutes, but for now, we can just look at the 24 minutes. Add 24 minutes to 57 part of sunrise, and you see that the sunset time must end in a 21. We see that the only option that ends with 21 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec86c9e7c664c2adedb2bc49d2f35fe1d5d2ae5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies  \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5:21\\textsc{pm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"156\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/v0SDWGo1_nU\">https://youtu.be/v0SDWGo1_nU</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 8\">2012 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1